+
+## Selection evidence audit (P-001, agent 01, run 43724282721, 2026-11-15)
+
+**Question.** Does the current focused-task selector improve learning efficiency relative to the repository's prior opportunistic task choice?
+
+**Verified selector mechanics** (read-only inspection of `.github/scripts/campaign_controller.py::task_rank` / `select_task`): selection is a deterministic ordinal ranking over seven *self-declared* labels (expected_information_gain, downstream_leverage, falsification_power, verifiability, effort, complexity, execution_risk), tie-broken by `task_id`; one task per agent; role-matched; the previous agent's decision propagates status (USEFUL_CHANGE / VERIFIED_NEGATIVE_RESULT / RETAIN -> RESOLVED, REJECT -> REJECTED, otherwise DEFERRED) and its `candidate_tasks` are appended and de-duplicated by `task_id`. The observed P-001 contract's `compared_against` order [P-001, P-002, P-004, P-003, P-006] reproduces exactly from the declared labels, so the selector is reproducible and auditable.
+
+**Verified evidence gap.** The selector has exactly one realized selection: `campaign_status.json` holds one `selection_history` entry (agent 1 -> P-001), `state/campaign/runs/` holds no earlier run, and `global_agent_counter.json` is at campaign 1. There is no outcome observation, no counterfactual, and no measured-value ranking; the "highest-value" claim rests on labels, not on measured information gain.
+
+**Verified comparison that does exist (worker-level, not selector-level).** Before the frontier-first rule, eight recorded MA(20/60) activation sections in `state/STATE.md` (real-data pipeline, per-asset perturbation, AAPL/NVDA/universe regime-stability, per-asset t-statistic, AMZN/JPM deep-dive, regime-adaptive MA) worked one hypothesis lineage without closing it. After the rule, seven consecutive activations (37263008074, 37304873966, 37314710995, 37318950814, 37361000967, 37394344201, 37414038601) each closed one distinct cell with a decisive, independently verified verdict (six FALSIFIED, one SUPPORTED). Closures per activation: 0/8 -> 6/7.
+
+**Contradictory evidence (preserved).** The "no equivalent re-tests" phrase in the 2026-10-06 entry is overstated for the momentum cell. `research/checks/momentum_sweep.py` (lookback 3/5/10/20, added in 2dfc2df5) and `research/checks/momentum_lookback_sweep.py` (lookback 3/5/10, added in 5ce6d789) implement the same information objective, and only the latter has an artifact. `momentum_sweep_results.json`, `momentum_concentration.py`, `verify_momentum_sweep.py` and `momentum_concentration.json` were added in 1354bd7c (2026-10-05) but are absent from the working tree and from the controller's 2026-11-15T14:26:36Z capture; no deletion commit was found. Attribution is also confounded: the frontier era added the engine cross-check, concentration gate, and independent verifier at the same time.
+
+**Process decision: RETAIN (qualified).** Retain frontier-first focused-task selection: it is the only rule with observed closure evidence, and the controller implements it reproducibly with structural dedupe and status propagation. The controller-side selector's own efficiency advantage is UNVERIFIED (n=1, label-based ranking, lexical tie-break). Do not claim a measured selector advantage until a later campaign records a rank-1 selection whose cell closes decisively and compares that against the recorded rank order.
+
+**Next.** One bounded action: a later campaign agent verifies from `campaign_status.selection_history` that each selected task was the rank-1 OPEN task of its role at selection time, and whether its cell closed decisively.

